{"abstract":"Enteroaggregative Escherichia coli (EAEC) is an increasingly recognized pathogen associated with acute and persistent diarrhea worldwide. While EAEC strains are considered highly heterogeneous, aggregative adherence fimbriae (AAFs) are thought to play a pivotal role in pathogenicity by facilitating adherence to the intestinal mucosa. In this study, we optimized an existing multiplex PCR to target all known AAF variants, which are distinguished by differences in their pilin subunits. We applied the assay on a collection of 162 clinical Danish EAEC strains and interestingly found six, by SNP analysis phylogenetically distinct, strains harboring the major pilin subunits from both AAF/III and AAF/V. Whole-genome and plasmid sequencing revealed that in these six strains the agg3A and agg5A genes were located on a novel pAA plasmid variant. Moreover, the plasmid also encoded several other virulence genes including some not previously found on pAA plasmids. Thus, this plasmid endows the host strains with a remarkably high number of EAEC associated virulence genes hereby likely promoting strain pathogenicity.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Jønsson, Rie","Struve, Carsten","Boll, Erik J.","Boisen, Nadia","Joensen, Katrine Grimstrup","Sørensen, Camilla Adler","Jensen, Betina H.","Scheutz, Flemming","Jenssen, Håvard","Krogfelt, Karen Angeliki"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-735539"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Diarrhea","EAEC","Fimbriae","Virulence genes","enteroaggregative E coli"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel paa virulence plasmid encoding toxins and two distinct variants of the fimbriae of enteroaggregative escherichia coli","src":["ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2017.00263","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-735539","identifier":[{"id":"85014491495","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5320562","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28275371","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-9002daa0-efe4-4456-96bd-e3178624bea8","ruc-4679b5c2-1990-46d6-bf6e-6f099b444a7c"],"keyword":["EAEC","diarrhea","enteroaggregative E. coli","fimbriae","virulence genes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EF67C0C9960C549450ABD96D8382D47D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/111450385/fmicb-08-00263.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2017.00263","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Department of Immunology and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Rie","key":"jønssonpau","last":"Jønsson","locid":"cd1cc5e5-d680-4d05-8b0d-a0147338d56f","name":"Jønsson, Rie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Carsten","key":"struvepau","last":"Struve","name":"Struve, Carsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Erik J.","key":"bollpau","last":"Boll","name":"Boll, Erik J.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Nadia","key":"boisenpau","last":"Boisen","name":"Boisen, Nadia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Katrine Grimstrup","key":"joensenpau","last":"Joensen","name":"Joensen, Katrine Grimstrup","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Camilla Adler","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Camilla Adler","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Betina H","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"0ed62cb4-7806-45e3-a5dd-ee63eb282e12","name":"Jensen, Betina Hebbelstrup","name_org":"Jensen, Betina H","orcid":"0000-0003-4247-5920","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Flemming","key":"scheutzpau","last":"Scheutz","name":"Scheutz, Flemming","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","country":"dk","first":"Håvard","key":"jenssenpau","last":"Jenssen","locid":"4e5fb70f-7fa7-4a47-a55f-66a0c67d966a","name":"Jenssen, Håvard","orcid":"0000-0003-0007-0335","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Karen A","key":"krogfeltpau","last":"Krogfelt","locid":"e3b149db-5709-4505-9cd6-dd43ec01912c","name":"Krogfelt, Karen Angeliki","name_org":"Krogfelt, Karen A","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28275371"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmicb.2017.00263","issn":["1664302X"],"issue":"FEB","journal":"Frontiers in Microbiology","paperid":"263","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Microbiology","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85014491495"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9002daa0-efe4-4456-96bd-e3178624bea8","ruc-4679b5c2-1990-46d6-bf6e-6f099b444a7c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"A Novel pAA Virulence Plasmid Encoding Toxins and Two Distinct Variants of the Fimbriae of Enteroaggregative Escherichia coli","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-735539","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Statement of context: The Danish Health Authority recommends that patients with brain tumours should have their rehabilitation needs evaluated prior to hospital discharge. Critical reflection on practice: To our knowledge, no specific recommendations for specialised occupational therapy intervention in patients with glioma have been published. We rationalise how occupational therapy practices founded on shared decision-making and common goal-setting are implicated to patients with brain tumours and elaborate on how an occupation-centred approach with occupation-focused and based intervention has the potential to impact a patient’s performance ability and satisfaction in performing occupations established by the Canadian Occupational Performance Measure. This practice was embedded in a randomised controlled trial investigating the effectiveness of intensive rehabilitation efforts and involving occupational therapy compared with standard care in patients with glioma (ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier NCT02221986). Implications for practice: Occupational therapy makes an important contribution in neurorehabilitation, which may also apply to patients with brain tumours.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hansen, Anders","Boll, Mette","Rosenbek Minet, Lisbeth Kirstine","Søgaard, Karen","Kristensen, Hanne Kaae"],"cuid":["S03-094.16-742472"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Brain tumour","Glioma","Occupational Therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"novel occupational therapy intervention in the early rehabilitation of patients with brain tumours","src":["sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/0308022617714165","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-094.16-742472","identifier":[{"id":"85030316521","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-fe59e474-b2ca-4f4e-8814-f3e354bfde9a","ucl-063312d0-1991-4611-a775-bff7fd887e89","ucl-49905e8c-c4e2-4221-92cf-89cf8535429b"],"keyword":["Brain tumour","glioma","occupational therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-E2896F919BE55CF66C791C8C4427AF0F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/0308022617714165","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, Rehabilitation","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Ergoterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO