{"abstract":"The article investigates an instance of responsive regulation as a team of inspectors conducts an unannounced raid. The raid takes place in Denmark and its aim is to judge and regulate tax compliance in a number of small businesses. The article argues that different ‘logics of generalization’ is at play as inspectors as well as business owners value the state-­of-­affairs in the businesses. Furthermore, the article discusses how the inspectors are responsive in the raid. It argues that they are responsive – not primarily towards the behaviour of the taxpayers – but towards a general public. The article hereby engages in the debate concerning what responsive regulation is and how it is played out in practice as the state regulates citizens and businesses. The overall analytical framework is inspired by Helen Verran’s notion of ‘relational empiricism’, and the analysis is an example of how this analytic can be used as a heuristic to analyze ethnographic data.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Boll, Karen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382874"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Logics of generalization","Relational empiricism","Responsive regulation","Tax compliance","Unannounced raid"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the responsive raid an analysis of the dual logics of generalization in judging businesses tax compliance and in doing responsive regulation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382874","ids":["itu-6be46a99-bebd-43e5-b5f5-2d2e655f1be6"],"keyword":["Logics of generalization","Relational empiricism","Responsive regulation","Tax compliance","Unannounced raid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8449B935B54D323B810D3AF29CDEDA4C"],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"bollpau","last":"Boll","locid":"59042bb8-c701-462c-990b-ce3d8006fd84","name":"Boll, Karen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["11272252"],"journal":"Encounters","status":"p","title":"Encounters","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6be46a99-bebd-43e5-b5f5-2d2e655f1be6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Responsive Raid – An Analysis of the Dual Logics of Generalization in judging Businesses’ Tax Compliance and in doing Responsive Regulation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382874","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"At højne regelefterlevelsen er i høj kurs, men hvordan gør man bedst dette? SKAT har udarbejdet en ny bærende strategi, og der er kommet meget ny forskning indenfor skatteadfærd. Kan dette hjælpe SKAT? ErhvervsPhD-stipendiat, Karen Boll, kigger på de nye trends. Baseret på sin afhandling skriver Karen hen over de næste tre numre af SKATTE-fagligt om sin forskning. Dette er den første artikel i serien.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Boll, Karen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-282926"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"den t formede skattemedarbejder","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-282926","ids":["cbs-4f1bfe28-3df6-4aa9-89cd-ae09d2317bd1"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A5D459E7162B58433E92C3F9332380DE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karen","key":"bollpau","last":"Boll","locid":"ea9574f1-23ef-4b7a-956c-dafe20986b54","name":"Boll, Karen","orcid":"0000-0001-9497-4372","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["22449388"],"issue":"5","journal":"Skattefagligt","pages":"21-23","publisher":"SRF Skattefaglig Forening","status":"p","title":"Skattefagligt"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-4f1bfe28-3df6-4aa9-89cd-ae09d2317bd1"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Den T-formede skattemedarbejder","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-282926","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
